  <title>Introducing Eletre X Hybrid </title>
  <link rel="alternate" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GEmlq5E5BqU"/>
  <author>
   <name>Lotus Cars</name>
   <uri>https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC9MkdpqU8D6xT1Z9A7dBlKg</uri>
  </author>
  <published>2026-06-18T11:00:01+00:00</published>
  <updated>2026-10-26T09:29:30+00:00</updated>
  <media:group>
   <media:title>Introducing Eletre X Hybrid </media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/GEmlq5E5BqU?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/GEmlq5E5BqU/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>The next generation of Lotus performance. Eletre X was engineered around a simple principle: power that stays accessible, repeatable and effortless. 

The Lotus X Hybrid system combines high-output electric drive with intelligent onboard power generation. Electric motors deliver the propulsion, Instant torque, seamless power delivery.  An integrated generator works quietly in the background, maintaining available energy over longer distances. 

The responsiveness and performance expected of a Lotus while extending capability over distance.

Engineered for drivers who refuse to compromise:

-  Up to 952 PS
- 0–100 km/h (62 mph) in 3.3 seconds
- 900V architecture
- Up to 350 km (217 mi) electric range (WLTP target)
- Over 1,200 km (745 mi) combined range (WLTP target)
- 20–80% charge in approximately 9 minutes*

Available to order now across mainland Europe. Customer deliveries expected from Q4 2026.** 

UK availability later this year.

Visit www.lotuscars.com for more details.


*Stated charging times are based on the use of a 350 kW DC fast charger under optimal conditions and represent best-case scenarios.
**Eletre X shown with optional equipment. Target specifications, features, charging times, performance figures, range values and availability may vary by market and are subject to final homologation. WLTP figures are preliminary and pending certification. Charging times depend on charger type, vehicle condition, battery temperature and environmental factors. European deliveries expected from Q4 2026. UK availability later this year subject to right-hand-drive homologation. Please visit lotuscars.com for market-specific information and final specifications.</media:description>
